/E (Interview by Vice President AJ Wyckoff and Secretary Micah Shively. Edited by President Preston Koeninger.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 122 0 R
/T ( James Atkinson II grew up in Louisville and calls Kentucky Kingdom his home park. He started there as a ride operator in 2023. Now in his fourth season, he's the park's Marketing and Sales Coordinator, and he's a lifetime passholder. Atkinson spoke to THRILL members at ESSRB earlier this semester. This fall, AJ and Micah caught up with him at the park during Pumpkins at Kentucky Kingdom to talk about the fall lineup, his favorite coaster, and why UofL students should make the short drive over. This interview has been lightly edited for length and clarity. The full interview can be viewed on THRILL's social media at @thrill.uofl.)
/E ( James Atkinson II grew up in Louisville and calls Kentucky Kingdom his home park. He started there as a ride operator in 2023. Now in his fourth season, he's the park's Marketing and Sales Coordinator, and he's a lifetime passholder. Atkinson spoke to THRILL members at ESSRB earlier this semester. This fall, AJ and Micah caught up with him at the park during Pumpkins at Kentucky Kingdom to talk about the fall lineup, his favorite coaster, and why UofL students should make the short drive over. This interview has been lightly edited for length and clarity. The full interview can be viewed on THRILL's social media at @thrill.uofl.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 122 0 R
/T (Shively: What does the fall season have to offer at Kentucky Kingdom? )
/E (Shively: What does the fall season have to offer at Kentucky Kingdom? )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 122 0 R
/T (Atkinson: The fall season brings Pumpkins at Kentucky Kingdom. This is our fifth year having it. When Herschend Family Entertainment purchased the park in 2021, they really wanted more family events, so Pumpkins came in 2022 and Christmas at Kentucky Kingdom followed in 2024. This is also the first year we're home to the original Jack O'Lantern Spectacular, and it's included with admission. You don't pay extra. Twenty five phenomenally talented local carvers carve over 5,000 pumpkins by hand. We drained one of our two lazy rivers, which is a little more than a quarter mile long, and after dusk every night we're open, you walk the pumpkin trail around it and take it all in. All the rides are included too. You can ride Wind Chaser, Lightning Run, and the new Flying Fox at night. We have great food. My favorite is probably the pumpkin spice deep fried Oreos, and as you can tell, I've had enough of those already. Something new this year is a costume parade, where the little kids get to parade around the park. That's what we have to offer, and there's a lot more I could go on and on about. )
/E (Atkinson: The fall season brings Pumpkins at Kentucky Kingdom. This is our fifth year having it. When Herschend Family Entertainment purchased the park in 2021, they really wanted more family events, so Pumpkins came in 2022 and Christmas at Kentucky Kingdom followed in 2024. This is also the first year we're home to the original Jack O'Lantern Spectacular, and it's included with admission. You don't pay extra. Twenty five phenomenally talented local carvers carve over 5,000 pumpkins by hand. We drained one of our two lazy rivers, which is a little more than a quarter mile long, and after dusk every night we're open, you walk the pumpkin trail around it and take it all in. All the rides are included too. You can ride Wind Chaser, Lightning Run, and the new Flying Fox at night. We have great food. My favorite is probably the pumpkin spice deep fried Oreos, and as you can tell, I've had enough of those already. Something new this year is a costume parade, where the little kids get to parade around the park. That's what we have to offer, and there's a lot more I could go on and on about. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
